{
	title: 'One batched redraw scheduler with navigable calls',
	spec: 'Redraw requests go through one frame scheduler: many requests in one frame paint once, and the paint is full if any request asked for a full repaint. Theme changes request a full repaint; content updates stay incremental. Go to definition from any redraw call reaches the code that schedules or paints: no empty placeholder functions overwritten at startup and no forwarding aliases (AGENTS.md Module initialization and navigation). Cyclic imports are allowed within layer boundaries; src/common must not pull the terminal renderer into the web bundle. terminal.redraw and the resize handler request through the scheduler. Suspended or external terminals are never painted; requests before the renderer starts do nothing. Reset cancels queued paints. A request during a paint schedules another frame. The result has less code than before. Web behavior is unchanged.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'render.request(full?: string) in src/client/render.ts is the one scheduler: a microtask paint, then at most one per frameMs; full is the e4c trigger, and one full request makes the batched paint full. terminal.redraw, terminal.onResize and src/common/rendering.ts are gone; Ctrl-L, theme preview, rebase editor close, resume and resize call render.request directly. theme-palette.ts moved to src/client: plugins and themes load in every Bun process (serve, print, remote, terminal) but never in the web bundle, and common may not import client; in a headless process render.state.out is null, so requests do nothing. render-view.draw also skips while suspended, so no request path paints over the shell. The microtask checks render.state identity so reset cancels it. redraw-trace now passes every argument to request/draw/paintParts (it had dropped the trigger and the rebuild callback). Checked in a tmux pty: theme plugin drop, Ctrl-L (one clear-down plus full write) and a resize repaint. Root README Request a redraw section still shows rendering.requestRedraw; README is user-owned.',
		'terminal.park, an empty placeholder that render.init replaced, is gone: terminal.leave calls render.park directly, which does nothing before render.init. Remaining placeholders of the same kind: terminal.onKeys, onQuit, onScreen.',
		'terminal.onKeys and terminal.onScreen, empty placeholders app.init replaced, are gone: terminal calls app.onKeys and app.sendScreen directly (both client; keys and resizes arrive only after main.initTerminal has run app.init). terminal.onQuit remains: main sets it to host.quitting, and client may not import host.'
	],
	needs: ['3jk'],
	foldInto: ['3jk']
}
